We need to let our app know to use this router when a user makes a request to the /trips endpoint. Let's update our server.js file to set this up.

In server.js:


Import the router from /routes/trips.js as tripRoutes.

import tripRoutes from './routes/trips.js'

After our middleware and before calling app.listen(), use app.use() to specify that the /trips endpoint should use the tripRoutes router. We'll add /api in front of the endpoint so we can set the server proxy for the frontend to /api when we set up the client.

app.use('/api/trips', tripRoutes)
This means when a user makes a request to a URL that has a path after the base URL that starts with /api/trips, the app will look into the tripRoutes module to resolve it.

